From 227cd689a0d729c99ef49ef1bf36807341dfb5d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:49:59 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 152/152] arm64: dts: exynos9810-gtactive3wifi: disable the C2
 idle states for now

The first Duranium boot with C2 available hung for good: PID 1 blocked
for >480 s in binder_init -> misc_register -> devtmpfs_create_node ->
wait_for_completion (photographed boot console). Cores that power down
in C2 are not woken again yet. Keep DVFS and the rest, drop C2 until the
PMU wake-up path is in place.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts  | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
index 79a3f8363..3da4f6d0b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dts
@@ -1748,3 +1748,18 @@ bluetooth: bluetooth {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Not yet: the PSCI core power-down (C2) states. On the device (Duranium
+ * 26102210, NO_HZ_IDLE) the boot hung with PID 1 blocked in
+ * devtmpfs_create_node: a core that entered C2 was never woken again,
+ * so the work queued on it never ran. The cluster's PMU wake-up events
+ * still need setting up before C2 can be used.
+ */
+&little_cpu_sleep {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&big_cpu_sleep {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
-- 
